    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239-a6">

                <pb facs="0573" n="483" xml:id="pg483"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 14 in No. 25.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Davis to Mr. Appleton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1874-09-25"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 25,
                    1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the23d September, respecting the claims to collect from yon an
                    income-tax. I shall transmit the correspondence to the Department of State for
                    instructions. But in case you are paying faxes on your personal property in
                    America, or in case you have paid income-tax to the United States, I think it
                    well to enable me also to inform the Department of the place of assessment and
                    payment of such taxes.</p>
                <p>Awaiting your reply, I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. C. B. DAVIS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">B. B. Appleton</hi>, Esq.,<lb/>10 (2) <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sidonian Sirasse, Dresden.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
